WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.852
Machine learning finds useful patterns in data, then applies them to new inputs.

00:00:04.852 --> 00:00:09.704
Examples pair inputs with expected outcomes so the system can learn patterns.

00:00:09.704 --> 00:00:14.556
The model compares examples and adjusts until its patterns become useful.

00:00:14.556 --> 00:00:19.408
A new order is an input; the learned pattern produces a prediction.

00:00:19.408 --> 00:00:24.260
Testing measures where predictions work—and where a person should review.

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:29.112
Machine learning learns from examples, then applies learned patterns to new inputs.
